1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:04,816
OK, Philip. This is your third cup of coffee.

2
00:00:04,816 --> 00:00:06,200
We should get to work,

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,600
or we won't be finished by dinnertime.

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,123
I guess we must.

5
00:00:10,123 --> 00:00:12,700
We must.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:23,156
OK. The beginning of my famous Thanksgiving apple pie.

7
00:00:23,156 --> 00:00:29,000
One apple. Two apples. Three apples. Four apples.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,800
Come on, Philip!

9
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,300
Get busy with your famous apple pie.

10
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,200
There's much more to be done.

11
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,300
Now, the ingredients.

12
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:36,000
What goes into my apple pie besides apples?

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:50,800
Ah, yes. Flour, sugar, butter.

14
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,938
Butter, nice and cold and hard.

15
00:00:53,938 --> 00:00:55,927
OK, here are the walnuts.

16
00:00:55,927 --> 00:00:57,100
Last but not least,

17
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,814
the reason my apple pie is famous--cinnamon.

18
00:01:01,814 --> 00:01:04,800
Cinnamon ...

19
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,751
Ellen, where's the cinnamon?

20
00:01:06,751 --> 00:01:06,951
If there is any cinnamon,

21
00:01:06,768 --> 00:01:18,400
it's in the cabinet with the salt and pepper.

22
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:23,400
Salt, pepper, dill weed, garlic powder, cinnamon. Ellen?

23
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,100
Yes, Philip.

24
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:29,041
Is it possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon?

25
00:01:29,041 --> 00:01:33,969
Yes, it is possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon.

26
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:37,348
Well, how can I make my famous apple pie without cinnamon?

27
00:01:37,348 --> 00:01:38,100
Good morning.

28
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,100
Oh, hi, Robbie. Good morning.

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,800
Good morning. Robbie.

30
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,500
Can you do me a favor?

31
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,500
Sure, Dad. What?

32
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:47,700
Remember my apple pie on Thanksgiving?

33
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:51,800
What do you love about it?

34
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:52,300
The apples?

35
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,596
No. The sssss...

36
00:01:54,596 --> 00:01:56,100
Cinnamon.

37
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:59,656
Right. We don't have any cinnamon.

38
00:01:59,656 --> 00:02:02,100
I'll go down to Henry's grocery. He's always open.

39
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,400
I'll get some for you.

40
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,900
That's my boy!

41
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:07,200
Oh, put your heavy jacket on, Robbie.

42
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:11,334
It's cold outside.

43
00:02:11,334 --> 00:02:13,300
Alexandra might call.

44
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,810
Tell her I'll call her right back.

45
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:16,700
OK.

46
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:20,800
Thanks, Son.

47
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:34,300
Uh, why does he always have to slam the door?

48
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:38,700
Hello.... Hello, Alexandra. How are you? ... Fine.

49
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,000
Robbie just went to the store.

50
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,700
He'll be back soon.

51
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:42,700
He said he'll call you.

52
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:48,600
... Oh, oh, I see.... Oh ... certainly. ...

53
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,600
Well, do you have the phone number there?

54
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:56,000
... Oh ... I see.... Please, I know he wants to talk to you.... ...

55
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,200
Thank you,

56
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,857
and happy Thanksgiving to you and your family, too.

57
00:02:59,857 --> 00:03:05,200
Try to come by later for dessert.... Bye.

58
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,140
That was Alexandra.

59
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,100
She and the Molinas

60
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:09,400
are going to spend Thanksgiving with their cousins.

61
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,130
She doesn't have the phone number.

62
00:03:11,130 --> 00:03:13,453
Oh, Robbie will be disappointed.

63
00:03:13,453 --> 00:03:15,400
He'll be grouchy.

64
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:19,710
Maybe she'll call back. She promised.

65
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:26,700
Here's your cinnamon, Pop.

66
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:31,400
It was a dollar and sixty cents.

67
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,500
You forgot to ask me for the change.

68
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:42,800
Or did you forget to give it to me?

69
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,900
Thanks, Son.

70
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,200
Alexandra called.

71
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,407
I'll call her back.

72
00:03:48,407 --> 00:03:49,859
She said she'll call you later.

73
00:03:49,859 --> 00:04:00,392
She's not at home.

74
00:04:00,392 --> 00:04:01,880
You should have your breakfast, Son.

75
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:03,437
Make you feel better.

76
00:04:03,437 --> 00:04:05,100
Protein, vitamins.

77
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,482
She said she'll call back?

78
00:04:06,482 --> 00:04:08,937
Yes, she did.

79
00:04:08,937 --> 00:04:10,310
Good morning, everyone!

80
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:13,223
Happy Turkey Day!

81
00:04:13,223 --> 00:04:14,000
What's wrong?

82
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,881
Nothing. Absolutely nothing.

83
00:04:18,881 --> 00:04:20,729
What's gotten into him?

84
00:04:20,729 --> 00:04:22,551
He missed a phone call.

85
00:04:22,551 --> 00:04:23,700
From ...?

86
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:27,100
Yes, Alexandra.

87
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:31,465
It's nice to see young love.... Oh, to be young again!

88
00:04:31,465 --> 00:04:34,465
Where's the coffee?
